<body>
    <%- include('partials/site-nav') %>

    <main class="container">
        <div class="card">
            <h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
            <p class="muted">Find answers to common questions about Stackdrop and Stackdrop Pro.</p>
            
            <div class="search-box">
                <input type="text" id="faq-search" placeholder="Search FAQ..." onkeyup="searchFAQ()">
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="category-section">
            <h2 class="category-title">Getting Started</h2>
            
            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">What is Stackdrop and how does it work?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Stackdrop is a Windows software installer generator that creates silent installers for multiple applications. You select the apps you want from our comprehensive list, and Stackdrop generates a single executable that downloads and installs all selected software silently without user interaction. This saves time and eliminates the need to manually install each application individually.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">Is Stackdrop free to use?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Yes, the basic Stackdrop installer generator is completely free. You can generate installers for as many applications as you want without any cost. Stackdrop Pro offers advanced features like device management, automatic updates, and bulk operations for $2.99/month (up to 20 PCs) or $14.99/month (up to 100 PCs).
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">What operating systems does Stackdrop support?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Stackdrop works on Windows 7, 8, 8.1, 10, and 11, including equivalent Server versions. The installer automatically detects your system architecture and installs the appropriate 64-bit or 32-bit versions of applications. It also respects your system's language settings.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="category-section">
            <h2 class="category-title">Installation & Usage</h2>
            
            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">How do I use Stackdrop?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Using Stackdrop is simple: 1) Visit our homepage and select the applications you want to install, 2) Click "Get Your Stackdrop Installer" to generate the installer, 3) Download and run the generated EXE file, 4) The installer will automatically download and install all selected applications silently. If Windows SmartScreen appears, click "More info" then "Run anyway".
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">What happens if Windows SmartScreen blocks the installer?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Since we're a new website, Windows SmartScreen may briefly warn you while our reputation builds. This is normal and expected. Simply click "More info" and then "Run anyway" to proceed. Stackdrop installers are generated on-demand and use vendors' official download links, so they're completely safe.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">Can I customize installation options?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Stackdrop installs applications with their default settings and locations. For advanced customization options like custom installation paths, pre/post installation scripts, and granular control over each application, you'll need <a href="/pro">Stackdrop Pro</a>.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="category-section">
            <h2 class="category-title">Troubleshooting</h2>
            
            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">How do I troubleshoot installation issues?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    If installations fail, try these steps: 1) Check your firewall and antivirus settings - they may be blocking downloads, 2) Ensure you have stable internet connectivity, 3) Try generating a new installer with fewer apps to isolate the problematic application, 4) Contact us through the <a href="/feedback">feedback page</a> with specific error messages for personalized help.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">Why do some applications prompt for user input?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Most applications are configured for silent installation, but some may still prompt for user input. If you encounter this, please report it through our <a href="/feedback">feedback page</a> so we can update the installation parameters for that specific application.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">What if an application fails to install?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    If a specific application fails to install, the installer will continue with the remaining applications. Failed installations are usually due to network issues, insufficient permissions, or the application already being installed. You can re-run the installer or generate a new one focusing on the failed applications.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="category-section">
            <h2 class="category-title">Stackdrop Pro</h2>
            
            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">What is Stackdrop Pro and what features does it offer?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Stackdrop Pro is a professional software management dashboard that provides: automatic app updates across all managed PCs, one-click bulk installs and removals, live device monitoring with hostnames and last-seen times, customizable install scripts with pre/post hooks, Windows tray client with background updates, and a modern web dashboard for centralized management.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">How much does Stackdrop Pro cost?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Stackdrop Pro offers two pricing tiers: Starter plan at $2.99/month for up to 20 PCs, and Pro plan at $14.99/month for up to 100 PCs. Both plans include all Pro features. For larger deployments (200+ PCs), we offer volume pricing - contact us through the <a href="/feedback">feedback page</a> for custom pricing.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">Can I try Stackdrop Pro before subscribing?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Yes! You can create a free account and explore the Pro dashboard features. The basic installer generation remains free, and you can upgrade to a paid plan when you're ready to manage multiple devices or need the advanced features.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="category-section">
            <h2 class="category-title">Technical Details</h2>
            
            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">How often are application versions updated?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Our system scans for application updates daily at 3am UTC. We also manually trigger updates when new versions are released. The installer always downloads the latest stable version of each application from the vendor's official website.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">Are the downloads secure and verified?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Yes, all downloads are verified for digital signatures or checksums before execution. We only use official download links from application vendors, ensuring you get authentic, malware-free software. The installer also verifies each download before running it.
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="card faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question">What applications are supported?</div>
                <div class="faq-answer">
                    Stackdrop supports hundreds of popular Windows applications including web browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Opera), media players (VLC, iTunes, Spotify), security tools (Malwarebytes, Avast, AVG), development tools (Visual Studio Code, Python, Java), productivity software, and many more. The list is constantly growing based on user requests.
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <h3>Still have questions?</h3>
            <p>If you can't find the answer you're looking for, we're here to help!</p>
            <p>
                <a href="/feedback" class="btn btn-primary">Contact Support</a>
                <a href="/help" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Help Center</a>
            </p>
        </div>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <div class="container">
            <p class="muted">© <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> Stackdrop</p>
            <p style="margin-top:4px;margin-bottom:0;"><span class="text-muted" style="font-size: 12px;color:#999;">Views: <%= typeof viewCount !== 'undefined' ? viewCount : '' %></span></p>
            <%- include('partials/social-follow') %>
        </div>
    </footer>

    <script>
        function searchFAQ() {
            const searchTerm = document.getElementById('faq-search').value.toLowerCase();
            const faqItems = document.querySelectorAll('.faq-item');
            
            faqItems.forEach(item => {
                const question = item.querySelector('.faq-question').textContent.toLowerCase();
                const answer = item.querySelector('.faq-answer').textContent.toLowerCase();
                
                if (question.includes(searchTerm) || answer.includes(searchTerm)) {
                    item.style.display = 'block';
                } else {
                    item.style.display = 'none';
                }
            });
        }
    </script>
</body>
